<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<worksheet>
  <title>Post-Exam Self-Reflection</title>

  <page>
    <exercise>
      <p>
        How much time did you spend preparing for the exam?
      </p>
    </exercise>

    <exercise>
      <p>
        How did you distribute your workload (in %) between working by yourself and
        working with others?
      </p>
    </exercise>

    <exercise>
      <p>
        How did you distribute your workload (in %) between reading class notes,
        reworking old homework problems, trying new problems, and reading the book?
        You may add any other strategies you used here.
      </p>
    </exercise>

    <exercise>
      <p>
        What was difficult about the exam? Be specific: did you have trouble identifying 
        concepts, translating physics into math, doing algebra, or what?
      </p>
    </exercise>

    <exercise>
        <p>
            (Optional, but I recommend it) Annotate your exam and correct your mistakes. Upload
            a corrected version of your test.
        </p>
    </exercise>

    <exercise>
      <p>
        Identify one specific, actionable decision you could take this week to
        improve for your next exam.

        An <q>actionable</q> decision means it should be specific enough to be
        clear if you are succeeding at following it.
        <q>Study better</q> or <q>Be more careful about X</q> is vague.
        <q>Find 4 problems online with a nontrivial-looking constraint and practice writing it mathematically</q>
        <mdash/> this is actionable.
      </p>
    </exercise>

    <exercise>
      <p>
        Is there anything you want additional feedback on?
      </p>
    </exercise>

    <exercise>
      <p>
        Is there anything you'd like to share with me about the course, or about
        how you're doing?
      </p>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>